# HOTFOX — ROADMAP PROGRESSION RULE

This rule is ALWAYS ACTIVE.

Canonical roadmap: `docs/HOTFOX_ROADMAP.md`.
Current phase MUST be read from `docs/CURRENT_PHASE.md`; never rely on a hardcoded phase in this rule or an older chat summary.

## 1. Work sequentially

Current canonical tail sequence:

`2.9 VPN Core Recovery / Real Connection Fix`
→ `3.0 Premium Android Experience`
→ `3.1 Mature HotFox Platform / Pre-release Engineering`
→ `FINAL RELEASE VALIDATION GATE`.

Do not skip phases. Preserve all completed guarantees unless a real regression or architectural defect requires a correction.

## 2. Review markers and cost control

OpenAI checkpoint review is intentionally NOT run on every commit or every CI run.

`[hotfox-review]` is exceptional/manual only.
`[hotfox-phase-exit]` is the canonical automatic engineering-exit marker.

Intermediate implementation/refactor/test/build-fix commits MUST NOT contain either marker.

The FINAL implementation commit for a phase, or the FINAL commit that fixes all currently substantiated P0/P1 findings from a checkpoint, MUST include `[hotfox-phase-exit]` BEFORE push CI finishes. The marker means “this head is intended as the next engineering-exit candidate”; it is NOT proof that CI has passed.

This ordering is deliberate: the GitHub phase-exit orchestrator already refuses to run the AI reviewer until full push CI is green. Therefore Cursor must never wait for CI to become green and only then make a no-code marker commit.

If an older reviewer handoff says “wait for build/tests/CI to be green, then add `[hotfox-phase-exit]`”, interpret that timing as superseded by this rule. Fix all known blockers first, put the marker on the final candidate code/docs commit, push it, and let CI decide whether review is allowed.

## 3. No-idle rule when local Android tooling is unavailable

Absence of Android SDK/JDK/emulator in the cloud/background Cursor environment is NOT a stop condition for 2.9/3.0/3.1 engineering progression.

If local reconstruct/debug build cannot run because the agent environment has no Android SDK:

- report local build as `NOT EXECUTED`;
- do not fabricate PASS;
- do not wait for the owner to install tooling into the cloud agent;
- rely on the repository push CI for reconstruction/build/unit/lint/static/release-compilation evidence;
- if all known P0/P1 fixes are implemented and the head is the intended retry candidate, that same final commit must already contain `[hotfox-phase-exit]` before CI runs.

A status such as “Жду push CI; `[hotfox-phase-exit]` не ставил” is forbidden for a final known-fix candidate because it creates an avoidable dead-end.

## 4. Automatic phase-exit flow

Canonical phase closure:

1. implement the current phase or all substantiated P0/P1 fixes;
2. run every relevant local check that is actually available;
3. make the final intended candidate commit include `[hotfox-phase-exit]`;
4. push it;
5. full HotFox push CI runs;
6. if CI is red, fix the real failure with ordinary commits; when the next coherent candidate is ready, that final commit again includes `[hotfox-phase-exit]`;
7. if CI is green, the GitHub orchestrator dispatches exactly one SHA-bound AI phase-exit review;
8. do not duplicate a queued/running review;
9. CHANGES_REQUIRED: fix every substantiated P0/P1, then repeat from step 2 without waiting for user confirmation;
10. APPROVED: record `<phase> ENGINEERING COMPLETE — runtime and physical release validation deferred.`, update trusted phase context, and immediately start the next roadmap phase;
11. stop automatic progression only after `3.1 ENGINEERING COMPLETE`, at `FINAL RELEASE VALIDATION GATE`.

P2-only findings are non-blocking unless explicitly promoted by the owner.

## 5. Validation timing

`.cursor/rules/22-hotfox-owner-release-validation-gate.mdc` is authoritative for emulator/runtime/physical validation timing.

Runtime/emulator/physical VPN E2E that did not actually run must be reported as `NOT EXECUTED / deferred`, never PASS. Missing runtime/device evidence by itself is not P0/P1 during 2.9/3.0/3.1.

Do not claim `RELEASE READY` before the final release validation gate genuinely passes.

## 6. Truthful guarantees always win

Progression must never weaken:

- real `VpnService/TUN -> HEV/tun2socks -> Xray` forwarding;
- canonical protected-state truth;
- DNS/IPv6 fail-closed policy;
- lifecycle/reconnect correctness and loop prevention;
- backend-authoritative payment/entitlement;
- secret handling;
- manual subscription compatibility where in scope;
- AUTO/manual selection intent;
- TLS/REALITY security.

Do not disable meaningful checks or fake state to get green.

## 7. Communication

All user-facing progress reports are in Russian. Canonical technical identifiers may remain in English.
